# xsched-native-level2-source-sync: final chain step, level2-era deltas
# that existed only in the successful live HAL source and had no
# published patch. Applying this as the last patch of the native chain
# makes the prepared tree byte-identical to that source for every file
# the chain touches (verified: live level2-build/.output/hal-native
# -20260908.i8na51/source; cmp on the two files below).
#
# instruments carried (no upstream or earlier-chain content is touched):
#   platforms/cuda/hal/src/level2/instrument.cpp
#     - ToolPrepare renamed ToolPublish: the same plain dlsym of
#       xg_host_publish but single-argument (the gate-tool ABI the
#       successful runs used); the three ToolPublish call sites replace
#       the prepare(ctx, func, dev) plus trailing zero-call pairs;
#     - launch_mtx_ lock/unlock dropped around the direct-launch actuator
#       and publish pairs (InstrumentContext::Launch holds launch_mtx_
#       already for the relay path; the removed pairs were around
#       ToolPrepare in the original-entry path);
#     - xg2/xg3 bounded (512) debug counters and the XG2
#       Deactivate/Reactivate/Launch logs dropped;
#     - at-create preempt buffer header MemsetD8Async + StreamSynchronize
#       dropped from InstrumentManager::Create;
#     - includes: <atomic> no longer needed, <cstdlib> moved below
#       <cstring>.
#   platforms/cuda/hal/src/level2/cuda_queue.cpp
#     - Reactivate(): the NVBit-era CtxPushCurrent_v2 context push/pop
#       around the replay loop is removed; Reactivate runs on the
#       caller's context again, matching the native gate-tool flow.
#
# Apply AFTER native/xsched-native-meta-extend.patch (see
# native/README.md "Reproducible source preparation" and
# native/prepare_native_source.sh). patch -p1, plain.
--- a/platforms/cuda/hal/src/level2/instrument.cpp
+++ b/platforms/cuda/hal/src/level2/instrument.cpp
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
